;; Parser conformance corpus: each case's markup is parsed BOTH by
;; `htmldom.core/parse-into-document` and by a real Blink browser (Chrome;
;; Brave is the same engine), and the two resulting TREES are compared on
;; shape -- element tag names and nesting depth in document order, plus text
;; nodes normalised for whitespace, plus comments.
;;
;; The browser parses each case with `innerHTML` on a detached <div>, which
;; is the HTML fragment parsing algorithm with a <div> context element --
;; the same job `parse-into-document` does. See conformance/README.md.
;;
;; A FAILING CASE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BUG REPORT. This parser openly
;; says it is not WHATWG-compliant, and several groups here are known,
;; documented scope cuts (comments have no node type in kotoba.wasm.dom at
;; all; the adoption agency's furthest-block path is deferred to L3; there
;; is no html/head/body synthesis). They are in the corpus precisely so the
;; number tells the truth about them.
;;
;; Keep the markup EXACT: incidental indentation inside a case's html string
;; becomes real whitespace text nodes in both trees. Whitespace is only
;; present where a case is deliberately testing it.

[;; ---- tables: implied tbody, optional end tags, foster parenting -------

 {:id :table/implied-tbody
  :group :table
  :html "<table><tr><td>a</td></tr></table>"}

 {:id :table/implied-tbody-two-rows
