 ;; Which START TAGS take the "reconstruct the active formatting elements"
 ;; step. After the `</div>` the <em> is in the active formatting list but
 ;; off the stack of open elements, so a tag that reconstructs lands INSIDE
 ;; a reopened <em> and one that does not stays a sibling at depth 0 --
 ;; which makes these the discriminator for `no-reconstruct-start-tags`.
 ;; The two below are the COUNTEREXAMPLES: <xmp> closes a <p> exactly like
 ;; the <pre>/<listing> rule beside it and <button> closes a button, yet
 ;; both spec rules list the reconstruct step and a browser takes it. They
 ;; are here so that over-applying the exemption to "everything that closes
 ;; something" is a measured failure rather than an invisible one.

 {:id :fmt/xmp-still-reconstructs
  :group :formatting
  :html "<div><em>x</div><xmp>y</xmp>z"}

 {:id :fmt/button-still-reconstructs
  :group :formatting
  :html "<div><em>x</div><button>y</button>z"}

